cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "primus-paleo: simulation and track-identification framework for cosmic-ray paleo-detectors"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/cgalelli/primus-paleo"
abstract: >-
  Code for the PRImuS paleo-detector project. The primus_paleo Python package
  simulates nuclear-recoil track spectra in minerals from past cosmic-ray fluxes:
  cosmic-ray muons, neutrons and protons with their secondary cascades, atmospheric
  neutrinos, spontaneous fission and radiogenic neutrons, through the overburden and
  flux history of a sample, with track annealing and the etching and slicing of
  the resulting spectra. It comes with the Geant4 application that produces the
  particle-interaction simulations it reads, flux templates computed with MCEq, the
  OptimusPrimus deep-learning pipeline for track identification in optical microscopy
  images, and the notebooks reproducing the figures of the associated analyses.
  Simulation outputs are not included but can be regenerated with the provided code.
keywords:
  - paleo-detectors
  - cosmic rays
  - atmospheric neutrinos
  - nuclear recoil tracks
  - Geant4
  - MCEq
  - deep learning
  - track detection
